 "adaptations": [
  "Preserve all original source object counts, actor poses and passive ownership.",
  "Source-equivalent forms share a variant only when their source geometry and rear-wall fit match.",
  "Rubber plant retains six source-sized leaves and their node heights; tapered living stem, radial leaf directions and curved blades replace the legacy post and aligned discs. Fine existing catalogue nickel and dark moulded bakelite replace oversized galvanized and pebbled finishes locally.",
  "Slice 8 of the V2 environment dossier adds the hall stand (DomesticObject16) to the seventeen apartment vestibules, standing clear of every leaf's swing and switch approach; the sixteen V1 records are unchanged.",
  "Slice 11 of the V2 environment dossier adds a second reel deck (DomesticObject04) on 5B's deck table; it bears on that table like 2A's on the coffee table.",
  "Slice 12 of the V2 environment dossier adds two pinboards (4B's case wall, 5A's plan wall) and a wall-art form (artframe: stretched canvas with painted fields and edge tacks, or a moulded frame holding a document with a brass seal) for 5C's diptych and the framed pairs in 4A and 1A.",
  "Slice 13 of the V2 environment dossier adds cloth: a garment rail (header board, brackets, rail, garments on wooden hangers, optional repair tags) and a hung moving blanket (batten, bound edges, quilted rows), with five tinted cloth keys on the catalogue linen.",
  "Slice 14 of the V2 environment dossier puts one object in each of the eighteen private halls by the resident's routine: a lidded wicker hamper (new form), a galvanised boot tray with galoshes (new form) or a copy of an existing crate, each against a wall clear of every door and opening approach.",
  "Slice 15 of the V2 environment dossier adds a photograph style to the wall-art form (a toned print under a mat) and hangs wall art in 2C, 3D, 3A and 5B, with 2A's caption wall as a 1.2 x 0.9 m pinboard.",
  "Slice 17 of the V2 environment dossier adds a suitcase form (a leather case on its edge with straps, brass feet and a handle) for 4D's luggage in the vestibule.",
  "Slice 18 of the V2 environment dossier adds four studio forms: a treadle sewing machine (2B), a radio teardown on newspaper (3B), an easel with a blank canvas and a stack of six failed canvases face to the wall (5C).",
  "Slice 19 of the V2 environment dossier adds a card-index cabinet form (twelve drawers, brass pulls and blank label frames, one brass lock plate) for 6C's archive.",
  "Slice 20 of the V2 environment dossier adds a backdrop rail (header, brackets, rail, paper roll and hanging sheet) and a print line (two hook plates, a string, six pegged contact sheets) for 6A's studio.",
  "Slice 21 of the V2 environment dossier adds the lobby noticeboard (a 1.2 x 0.9 m pinboard of 23 drifted notices) and the 1928 photograph (a copy of the photograph frame) beside the inner door.",
  "Slice 23 of the V2 environment dossier stores one household object against the back of sixteen basement bays (two stay padlocked and empty) and sets five wicker baskets along the laundry's north wall, all copies of existing forms.",
  "Slice 24 of the V2 environment dossier adds 3D's error-archive card index as a completion copy of 6C's card cabinet.",
  "Slice 25 of the V2 environment dossier adds a cable hook strip form (batten, five hooks, taped cable loops) and copies: a third reel deck on 2C's rig table, 4D's print over the settee, 6A's three archive crates under the desk wall.",
  "Slice 26 of the V2 environment dossier mounts 4C's colour board (a completion copy of 5C's) at its existing anchor.",
  "Slice 28 of the V2 environment dossier adds three forms for the ground-floor service rooms (the operator's headset on its hook, a coat on a wall hook, the night watch's folded camp cot) and a copy of 6A's cable coil as the cord pile under the house board.",
  "Slice 29 of the V2 environment dossier adds five basement forms: the boiler room's leaning coal shovel, the clinker rake on two nails, the lidded ash can with an oil can on a rag, the Vantry signal frame (terminal strips, blank tag cards, cloth leads in a trunk cleated to the ceiling) and the steel conduit into and out of the fuse panel.",
  "Slice 32 of the V2 environment dossier adds eight service forms: an oil can on a rag, a spare belt on a nail and a folded stepladder in the basement laundry, a cast-iron umbrella stand in the vestibule, a brass spittoon in the lobby, and the staff restroom's soap dish, roller towel and mop bucket.",
  "Slice 33 of the V2 environment dossier adds three forms for the roof bulkhead (a coil of washing line, a watering can, a gardening trug) and 6A's row of three small prints as copies of 2C_album_a.",
  "Slice 34 of the V2 environment dossier adds the chimney sweep's soot sack and rod bundle inside the roof service bulkhead and 1A's trunk of lesson plans, a larger variant of the suitcase form.",
  "Slice 35 of the V2 environment dossier fills 2A's bedroom pinboard (DomesticObject00) to a full grid of 24 cards.",
  "Slice 37 of the V2 environment dossier adds a workboots form: 4B's pair of boots kicked off at the alcove bed's foot, one fallen against the other.",
  "Slice 38 of the V2 environment dossier adds a dressform form: Lena's tripod dress form in 2B wearing her own printed voile frock with a row of pins in the turned-up hem. voile is a tinted alias of the catalogue linen."
 ],
